WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.110 --> 00:00:04.400
Hey youtubers it's Charlie and since there
were so many Daleks in the Series 8 trailer

00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:07.450
that just posted I wanted to do a video for
my favorite Daleks. There have been over 13

00:00:07.450 --> 00:00:12.679
different people in the last 50 years to play
Daleks and if you count Dalek Oswin that number

00:00:12.679 --> 00:00:16.730
goes up to 14. In modern Doctor Who usually
Nicholas Briggs is credited with all the Dalek

00:00:16.730 --> 00:00:20.660
Voices, even variations on the normal Daleks
like the Prime Minister we saw in the Series

00:00:20.660 --> 00:00:21.670
7 opener.

00:00:21.670 --> 00:00:25.300
Hello any new people, if you're finding me
for the first time I do Doctor Who every week,

00:00:25.300 --> 00:00:30.730
be sure to subscribe to get everything. I've
got a lot of special stuff planned for when

00:00:30.730 --> 00:00:33.140
the episodes get here.

00:00:33.140 --> 00:00:37.420
So before I do my list here's a quick history
lesson on all the Dalek Voice actors. Most

00:00:37.420 --> 00:00:40.090
people just know about Nicholas Briggs but
there are a ton more.

00:00:40.090 --> 00:00:44.030
The high pitched Dalek Voice was created by
two actors named Peter Hawkins and David Graham

00:00:44.030 --> 00:00:49.470
for their first appearance in Season 1 episode
2, just called "The Daleks". The voice that

00:00:49.470 --> 00:00:53.470
they came up with was modified by Brian Hodgson
to give it that mechanical sound.

00:00:53.470 --> 00:00:56.700
You can actually watch a re-telling of them
doing this in Mark Gatiss' Adventure in Space

00:00:56.700 --> 00:01:01.489
in Time. The docu drama about the creation
of Doctor Who. If you haven't seen it, it's

00:01:01.489 --> 00:01:04.149
amazing, David Bradley plays William Hartnell.

00:01:04.149 --> 00:01:08.250
After those three people, there were 7 different
people who did Dalek Voices for brief periods

00:01:08.250 --> 00:01:11.080
before Nicholas Briggs took over in 2005.

00:01:11.080 --> 00:01:15.370
There have been 5 different voice actors to
voice Davros, who isn't technically a Dalek,

00:01:15.370 --> 00:01:20.159
but I usually include the character whenever
I talk about Daleks.

00:01:20.159 --> 00:01:24.470
Here are my top 10 Favorite Dalek characters.
This isn't a power ranking, it's just my own

00:01:24.470 --> 00:01:26.619
personal list of favorites:

00:01:26.619 --> 00:01:28.799
Starting with number 10 - Oswin Oswald Dalek

00:01:28.799 --> 00:01:32.130
This was a really fun twist on a Dalek and
I have to give it to Steven Moffat for trying

00:01:32.130 --> 00:01:36.880
to tell a Dalek story in a whole new way despite
Russell T Davies already having mined a lot

00:01:36.880 --> 00:01:39.460
of Humans as Daleks story material.

00:01:39.460 --> 00:01:43.759
It's still a big question mark in the series
and I'm hoping we get a call back to it in

00:01:43.759 --> 00:01:48.409
series 8. Supposedly Dalek Oswin was destroyed
when the Dalek Parliament destroyed the planet

00:01:48.409 --> 00:01:51.630
but it seems like whenever Time Travel is
possible and there are cracks in the universe,

00:01:51.630 --> 00:01:53.520
you never really die.

00:01:53.520 --> 00:01:59.140
The interesting thing about Dalek Oswin was
that supposedly she was one of the fractured

00:01:59.140 --> 00:02:03.630
reality Clara's that were created when Clara
Oswald jumped into the Doctor's Timestream

00:02:03.630 --> 00:02:05.509
in the series 7 finale.

00:02:05.509 --> 00:02:09.319
All of the versions of Clara seemed to retain
all the memories of the first version of clara.

00:02:09.319 --> 00:02:15.900
So if that were true, why did Dalek Oswin
not know the Doctor in Asylum of the Daleks.

00:02:15.900 --> 00:02:19.780
She seemed like she was learning about him
for the first time.

00:02:19.780 --> 00:02:23.730
The only explanation based on what we know
now, is that Oswin Oswald when she was still

00:02:23.730 --> 00:02:28.130
on the Alaska as a human, knew what was going
to happen. And then as a result of being converted

00:02:28.130 --> 00:02:30.720
into a Dalek, lost those memories.

00:02:30.720 --> 00:02:32.190
Number 9 - Davros from Genesis of the Daleks
(Michael Wischer)

00:02:32.190 --> 00:02:35.660
This is the Michael Wischer version of the
character. It's just fun to watch any of the

00:02:35.660 --> 00:02:41.060
classic Davros scenes since the style of writing
was so different. Because they didn't have

00:02:41.060 --> 00:02:44.400
the special effects or huge sets that you
see today all the action was in their crazy

00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:45.440
monologues.

00:02:45.440 --> 00:02:49.920
It's much more Davros as mad scientist, like
Frankenstein meets Doctor Who. So you spend

00:02:49.920 --> 00:02:56.920
a lot more time relying on your imagination
to conjure the things he's talking about.

00:03:02.430 --> 00:03:09.430
Now they can just show you, but sometimes
it's better when Davros just talks about tiny

00:03:10.019 --> 00:03:14.180
microscopic organisms reigning supreme and
your own brain hallucinates something epic

00:03:14.180 --> 00:03:21.180
that they could never do on a tv budget.

00:03:23.370 --> 00:03:25.790
Number 8 - Metaltron from Series 1

00:03:25.790 --> 00:03:30.170
This was the first new Dalek to be seen since
the 2005 reboot and the beginning of Russell

00:03:30.170 --> 00:03:35.450
T Davies love for humanizing the Daleks. Metaltron
was also the first new survivor of the Time

00:03:35.450 --> 00:03:40.440
War the Doctor found. Even though there ended
up being several more the Tenth Doctor met.

00:03:40.440 --> 00:03:45.080
I think this was also the first time we learned
Daleks could regenerate themselves by absorbing

00:03:45.080 --> 00:03:47.650
time energy. Rose explained to Mickey later
that they had evolved to use background Time

00:03:47.650 --> 00:03:48.599
Vortex radiation to restore themselves during
Doomsday.

00:03:48.599 --> 00:03:53.450
I loved how absorbing Human DNA started to
make them all go mad, just because they couldn't

00:03:53.450 --> 00:03:56.049
handle all the feels that came with Human
emotion.

00:03:56.049 --> 00:03:57.739
Number 7 - Prime Minister Dalek

00:03:57.739 --> 00:04:01.580
This was the one from Asylum, the Series 7
opener. I always love seeing the Khaled Mutants,

00:04:01.580 --> 00:04:03.420
everytime I see one I always think of Dalek
Caan, but really they're just what the organic

00:04:03.420 --> 00:04:07.049
The cool thing about the prime minister in
this episode was that he was begging the Doctor

00:04:07.049 --> 00:04:13.930
for help. Everytime we see Dalek's again you
can just feel the pressure to do something

00:04:13.930 --> 00:04:16.199
that hasn't been done before.

00:04:16.199 --> 00:04:21.099
The Doctor had worked alongside Daleks before,
but I can't remember the last time they asked

00:04:21.099 --> 00:04:23.279
him to save their race. Most of the time they're
just trying to kill him.

00:04:23.279 --> 00:04:27.539
And the big twist really ended up being him
getting erased from their memory banks. Even

00:04:27.539 --> 00:04:30.539
though they rediscovered his identity before
the Christmas Special last year.

00:04:30.539 --> 00:04:32.629
Number 6 - The new White Supreme

00:04:32.629 --> 00:04:37.039
This was Stephen Moffat's new take on the
Daleks, the New Dalek Paradigm. I should really

00:04:37.039 --> 00:04:41.499
include all of them in this one. Outwardly
they were most notable for the reskinned colors.

00:04:41.499 --> 00:04:46.210
Just because most of them previously had the
traditional gold look.

00:04:46.210 --> 00:04:51.089
The Daleks that created the new paradigm were
explained as survivors of the Medusa Cascade

00:04:51.089 --> 00:04:51.999
during the Tenth Doctor's run.

00:04:51.999 --> 00:04:56.279
I think they mostly followed up on the New
Paradigm daleks in the video game City of

00:04:56.279 --> 00:05:01.339
the Daleks.

00:05:01.339 --> 00:05:03.990
Number 5 - Dalek Emperor from Parting Of Ways

00:05:03.990 --> 00:05:08.729
This was the God Emperor of the Daleks. Which
kind of makes me think of God Emperor of Dune.

00:05:08.729 --> 00:05:12.779
The Frank Herbert Story. It's always cool
to see variations on the Dalek casings, his

00:05:12.779 --> 00:05:14.749
in this episode even had a little throne.

00:05:14.749 --> 00:05:21.009
It ended up being another twist on Daleks
as Humans with Human Emotional problems. The

00:05:21.009 --> 00:05:24.699
emperor got so crazy when Rose suggested that
the Daleks were part human because of all

00:05:24.699 --> 00:05:26.289
the dna they had harvested.

00:05:26.289 --> 00:05:31.029
He ended up creating an army of about 500
thousand Daleks that Rose was only able to

00:05:31.029 --> 00:05:36.580
destroy when she became the Bad Wolf entity.

00:05:36.580 --> 00:05:40.830
The emperor was so much fun mostly because
of the hubris. I mean, if a being really were

00:05:40.830 --> 00:05:45.969
perfect wouldn't it not care about anything
everyone else was doing or whether or not

00:05:45.969 --> 00:05:52.969
people acknowledged it as 
a god?

00:05:54.219 --> 00:05:59.629
Number 4 - Human Hybrid Dalek Sec
He was kind of a potential twist on the Davros

00:05:59.629 --> 00:06:03.960
character. Trying to fundamentally alter the
Dalek Race and make them all more human in

00:06:03.960 --> 00:06:05.029
a literal sense.

00:06:05.029 --> 00:06:08.849
I loved how he was awakened to this new reality
after being bonded to a human, started explaining

00:06:08.849 --> 00:06:13.039
his radical new theories to the Cult of Skaro
and they all kind of looked at each other

00:06:13.039 --> 00:06:15.439
and were like "Nope"! and vaporized him.

00:06:15.439 --> 00:06:21.099
It's a classic science fiction narrative that
anyone with new ideas immediately gets punished.

00:06:21.099 --> 00:06:23.979
Number 3 - Davros from Stolen Earth and Journey's
End

00:06:23.979 --> 00:06:28.949
This version of Davros was rescued from the
Time War by Dalek Caan. Previously Davros'

00:06:28.949 --> 00:06:34.169
mind had been sublimated by a Dalek consciousness.
So that he was Emperor of the Daleks, but

00:06:34.169 --> 00:06:39.499
there was a Dalek mind operating his body
and Davros' own consciousness was riding passenger.

00:06:39.499 --> 00:06:44.149
So when we see him for the first time in Stolen
Earth, he's just re-taken control of his mind

00:06:44.149 --> 00:06:49.399
and is working with the Daleks inside the
Medusa Cascade.

00:06:49.399 --> 00:06:56.399
Anytime Davros appears it seems like the stakes
have to be raised. This time it was destroying

00:06:56.740 --> 00:06:59.860
the multiverse so that only Daleks would be
left.

00:06:59.860 --> 00:07:04.949
I love how he cursed the Doctor as the greater
evil in the end. Like, yes I tried to destroy

00:07:04.949 --> 00:07:08.409
several universes, but you Doctor, are the
real villain.

00:07:08.409 --> 00:07:15.279
They used his speech in the last series 8
trailer, so it's hard to know how the series

00:07:15.279 --> 00:07:20.360
is going to deal with him going forward, since
the last we saw of him was in a fiery explosion

00:07:20.360 --> 00:07:21.219
on the crucible.

00:07:21.219 --> 00:07:23.899
Number 2 - The Dalek Genesis Ark

00:07:23.899 --> 00:07:27.969
This was technically not a Dalek itself, but
a device like the TARDIS that existed across

00:07:27.969 --> 00:07:32.309
dimensions and time and space housing a massive
army of Daleks.

00:07:32.309 --> 00:07:38.009
The reason they needed Rose or The Doctor
to open the ark was because it needed Time

00:07:38.009 --> 00:07:41.279
Radiation transmitted by touch and even though
the Daleks have khaled mutants inside them,

00:07:41.279 --> 00:07:42.589
they were supposedly incapable of touch.

00:07:42.589 --> 00:07:48.550
It's like a nuclear device that will explode
Daleks all over the world. Which is funny,

00:07:48.550 --> 00:07:52.679
because the master ended up using the TARDIS
in a similar way to bring the Toclafane to

00:07:52.679 --> 00:07:53.020
earth.

00:07:53.020 --> 00:07:56.809
They actually kind of remind me of Captain
Jack and his final Face of Boe form. Like

00:07:56.809 --> 00:08:03.809
everyone is destined for some horrific end.
and my Number 1 Dalek - Dalek Caan and the

00:08:04.259 --> 00:08:05.550
Cult of Skaro

00:08:05.550 --> 00:08:09.719
My favorite Dalek Caan appearance was in the
Stolen Earth Journey's end two parter. After

00:08:09.719 --> 00:08:16.149
he'd gone nutters. Caan is probably the most
interesting Dalek to me because he's a twist

00:08:16.149 --> 00:08:19.129
on Bad Wolf, minus the super powers.

00:08:19.129 --> 00:08:23.649
It's like he gained ultimate knowledge but
paid the ultimate price. Here's a timeline

00:08:23.649 --> 00:08:26.809
of events.

00:08:26.809 --> 00:08:30.909
We see him in Doomsday with the rest of the
Cult of Skaro trying to open the Genesis Ark.

00:08:30.909 --> 00:08:36.110
They fail and escape to New York in the 1930s.
They create Human Hybrid Dalek Sec but it

00:08:36.110 --> 00:08:38.599
goes sideways and Caan timeshifts out.

00:08:38.599 --> 00:08:43.129
He travels back to the first year of the Time
War being the first person to break the time

00:08:43.129 --> 00:08:48.350
lock. Saves Davros from the jaws of the Nightmare
Child and brings him to the Medusa Cascade.

00:08:48.350 --> 00:08:53.290
In the process of that rescue mission, he
sees all of time and space and goes mad.

00:08:53.290 --> 00:08:59.000
It's funny that the new Supreme during that
period called Caan an abomination.

00:08:59.000 --> 00:09:03.490
Let me know who your favorite Dalek is and
what twists on them you're expecting in series

00:09:03.490 --> 00:09:04.240
8.

00:09:04.240 --> 00:09:10.959
I'm going to post my next bonus video next
weekend or sooner if we get new footage before

00:09:10.959 --> 00:09:14.600
then. Be sure to subscribe to get everything.
They seem to be alternating casting news with

00:09:14.600 --> 00:09:15.480
new trailers.

00:09:15.480 --> 00:09:19.220
If you haven't seen it yet I just posted a
breakdown of the new Series 8 trailer. There

00:09:19.220 --> 00:09:23.069
are a lot of Daleks, including a Dalek battlecruiser.
Click here for that. And click here to see

00:09:23.069 --> 00:09:26.629
which other UK actors I'd like to see become
companions in the future.

00:09:26.629 --> 00:09:28.629
Thanks for watching, see you guys tonight,
high fives!

